Package: mscc
Version: 1.0.42
Section: hamradio
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Multus SDR / MSCC Linux <local@localhost>
Installed-Size: 1400
Depends: libc6, mscc-portaudio, libusb-1.0-0, libhidapi-libusb0, build-essential, kmod, udev, passwd, python3, python3-tk
Recommends: linux-headers-generic, pipewire-pulse | pulseaudio, pipewire, libnotify-bin, python3-pyaudio, pulseaudio-utils, alsa-utils
Homepage: https://local/mscc
Description: MSCC stack for Multus/Proficio on Ubuntu Desktop (amd64)
 Prebuilt MSCC servers (ms-sdr, sdrcore-recv, sdrcore-trans), mscc-init,
 Proficio firmware upload (bootloader CLI + GUI), start/stop script,
 Pulse/PipeWire virtual digi sinks (VirtualA/B), desktop menu
 Start/Stop/Status/Firmware Upload, and tty0tty null-modem module.
 Linked with rpath /usr/local against mscc-portaudio (Pulse+ALSA).
 Install mscc-portaudio_*_amd64.deb first. Do not use the Pi arm64 PortAudio .deb.
 .
 Supported platform: Ubuntu Desktop x86_64 (amd64) only.
 Raspberry Pi uses the arm64 mscc package instead.
 .
 Installs binaries into the installing user's $HOME/mscc, seeds
 $HOME/.local/mscc only when missing/empty, creates /usr/local/bin
 links, enables user service mscc-virtual-audio, and builds/loads tty0tty.
 .
 Desktop menu: MSCC Start / MSCC Stop / MSCC Status / Firmware Upload.
 Digi path: VirtualA (recv out) / VirtualB.monitor (trans digi mic).
 Kernel headers (linux-headers-generic) needed for tty0tty.
